<title>SWEDEN: Major owner says no comment on Astra talk.</title>
<headline>Major owner says no comment on Astra talk.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish investment company Investor AB, a major owner in drug firm Astra AB, on Thursday declined to comment on market rumours that Swiss drugs company Roche was interested in buying Astra.</p>
<p>&quot;We can not comment on this type of speculation,&quot; Investor spokesman Nils Ingvar Lundin told Reuters.</p>
<p>He said Investor, which owns 10 percent of the capital and 11.9 percent of the votes in Astra, had a long-term view on its ownership in the company and that Investor had recently increased its stake.</p>
<p>&quot;You can interpret that in your own way,&quot; Lundin said.</p>
<p>The Astra share rose eight crowns to 322.5 on the rumour, but at 1125 was trading at 320, up 5.5.</p>
<p>Astra has denied the rumour.</p>
<p>-- Joel Dahlberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1011</p>
</text>
